-- expect: 4:14: `&stdout` lends a capability to one call: it may appear only in the head `M` of `y <- M; N` (SPEC §11)
-- A lent capability comes back through a binding: `&stdout` in a `case`'s scrutinee has nowhere to go.
main : F 1 =
  case putb (&stdout, i32[104]) { inl u -> return () | inr u -> return () }
